module libraryQC
module sequencerReadyDetection

manifest GenomicDNA
manifest NexteraEnzymeMix
manifest PCRMixture
manifest MagneticBeads_SPRI
manifest EthanolWash
manifest ElutionBuffer
manifest PluronicF127
manifest FC40_Oil

// ============================================================
// A Microfluidic DNA Library Preparation Platform for
// Next-Generation Sequencing.
// Kim H, Jebrail MJ, Sinha A, et al.
// PLoS ONE 8(7): e68988 (2013).
// DOI: 10.1371/journal.pone.0068988
//
// Platform: Digital Microfluidics (DMF) hub with peripheral
//   capillary-based modules. Central DMF hub (185 um or
//   400 um gap, 48-electrode ITO array) routes droplets
//   via fused-silica capillaries to off-chip modules for
//   each unit operation.
//
// PROTOCOL OVERVIEW (Nextera workflow on DMF):
//   All DNA is prepared in TE buffer + 0.1% Pluronic F127
//   (w/v) to prevent biofouling on Teflon-AF coated surfaces.
//   Reagent boluses are moved at 10 uL/min by syringe pumps.
//   Driving potential: 80-90 V_rms at 15 kHz.
//
//   STEP 1:  Dispense gDNA sample (1.8 uL at 5 ng/uL) and
//            Nextera Enzyme Mix (0.6 uL) onto DMF hub; mix
//            by aspirating/dispensing in and out of capillary
//            for 30 s at room temperature.
//   STEP 2:  Tagmentation: aspirate into thermal module
//            (~850 um deep x 800 um wide trench in Al block)
//            and incubate at 55 C for 5 min. Transposase
//            simultaneously fragments and tags gDNA.
//   STEP 3:  Merge tagmented product with SPRI magnetic bead
//            droplet (4.5 uL) on DMF hub; aspirate into
//            clean-up module. External neodymium magnet
//            (3 mm dia x 3 mm thick) immobilises bead pellet.
//   STEP 4:  Wash bead pellet: dispense 3 uL ethanol onto
//            DMF hub, aspirate into clean-up module, shuttle
//            back-and-forth for 30 s; return to DMF, aspirate
//            to waste. Repeat wash twice (3 washes total).
//   STEP 5:  Elute DNA: dispense 2.2 uL elution buffer,
//            aspirate into clean-up module, remove magnet,
//            resuspend beads (30 s), re-apply magnet, return
//            eluate to DMF hub.
//   STEP 6:  Mix eluate (2.2 uL) with PCR Mixture (2.8 uL)
//            on DMF hub; aspirate 2.8 uL into PCR thermal
//            module (remaining 2.2 uL waste).
//            PCR conditions: 3 min 72 C init, 30 s 95 C
//            denaturation; 10 cycles (10 s 95 C, 30 s 62 C,
//            3 min 72 C). Adds sequencing adapters (Illumina).
//   STEP 7:  Size selection - Stage 1 (remove <200 bp):
//            merge PCR product with 2.2 uL SPRI beads,
//            aspirate into size-selection module.
//            Immobilise beads, return supernatant to DMF hub.
//   STEP 8:  Size selection - Stage 2 (remove >400 bp):
//            merge supernatant with 0.45 uL SPRI beads,
//            aspirate into size-selection module, ethanol
//            wash bead pellet; elute library (3 uL EB)
//            back onto DMF hub. Target library: 200-400 bp.
//   STEP 9:  QC detection: detect library signal on final
//            library droplet (Bioanalyzer / Kapa quant proxy).
//
// REAGENT VOLUMES (185 um-gap hub, human gDNA):
//   gDNA sample:        1.8 uL  (5 ng/uL in TE + 0.1% F127)
//   Nextera Enzyme Mix: 0.6 uL  (2 uL HMW + 0.5 uL enzyme mix)
//   SPRI beads clean-up: 4.5 uL
//   Ethanol wash:       3.0 uL  (repeated x3)
//   Elution buffer:     2.2 uL  (clean-up elution)
//   PCR Mixture:        2.8 uL  (12.5 uL 2X PCR buffer +
//                                0.5 uL primer cocktail +
//                                0.5 uL PCR enzyme +
//                                0.5 uL 50X Adapter 2)
//   SPRI beads SS1:     2.2 uL  (Stage 1: remove <200 bp)
//   SPRI beads SS2:     0.45 uL (Stage 2: remove >400 bp)
//   Elution buffer:     3.0 uL  (final library elution)
//
//   NOTE (400 um-gap hub, bacterial gDNA): all volumes 2X
//   except elution buffer (5 uL final); 9 PCR cycles used.
//
// NOTE ON PLURONIC ADDITIVE:
//   0.1% Pluronic F127 is added to all DNA and reagent
//   solutions to prevent biofouling (protein/enzyme adhesion
//   to Teflon-AF). Validated not to affect tagmentation
//   efficiency (Fig S1 in paper). Modelled here as a single
//   manifest; in practice it is pre-mixed into all solutions.
//
// NOTE ON MAGNETIC BEAD STEPS:
//   Wash and elution steps are implemented in peripheral
//   off-DMF capillary modules (not on the DMF electrode
//   array). `mix` statements model the bolus shuttle
//   mixing in the module tubing. Supernatant/waste removal
//   is modelled with `dispose`/`drain` per BioScript convention.
//
// NOTE ON HEAT STEPS:
//   Temperature control via closed-loop thermoelectric Al block.
//   BioScript `heat` duration tokens: s (seconds), m (minutes).
//   All durations converted accordingly.
//
// NOTE ON CONTAMINATION PREVENTION:
//   Between library runs the system is rinsed with 10% (v/v)
//   bleach and then deionized water (off-chip; not modelled).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main            -- entry: dispense, tagmentation,
//                           bead clean-up, PCR, size-selection
//   BB2  libraryPass     -- librarySignal > 0: valid library
//                           (200-400 bp); dispose for sequencing
//   BB3  libraryFail     -- librarySignal <= 0: failed library;
//                           drain
//   BB4  finalCleanup    -- terminal: dispose QC signal;
//                           library ready for MiSeq loading
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1a: Dispense gDNA sample (1.8 uL, 5 ng/uL in TE
//   buffer + 0.1% Pluronic F127). Sample dispensed from
//   pre-loaded capillary onto the 185 um-gap DMF hub at
//   160 V_rms, 15 kHz driving potential.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

gdnaDroplet     = dispense 1 units of GenomicDNA

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1b: Dispense Nextera Enzyme Mix (0.6 uL) from its
//   capillary onto the DMF hub. Mix contains 2 uL High
//   Molecular Weight component + 0.5 uL enzyme mix +
//   0.1% Pluronic F127 to prevent biofouling (Fig S1).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nexteraEnzyme   = dispense 1 units of NexteraEnzymeMix

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1c: Mix gDNA + Nextera Enzyme on DMF hub.
//   Active mixing (30 s, room temperature) achieved by
//   continuously aspirating and dispensing the merged droplet
//   in and out of the capillary. The mixed droplet is then
//   aspirated into the tagmentation thermal module.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tagmentationMix = mix gdnaDroplet with nexteraEnzyme for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Tagmentation - incubate at 55 C for 5 min.
//   Mixed droplet aspirated into the tagmentation module
//   (750 um OD tubing recessed ~100 um below the surface
//   of a custom Al block; temperature match within ~5 C).
//   Transposase simultaneously fragments and adapter-tags
//   gDNA. Product: adapter-tagged DNA fragments (150-1000 bp
//   broad distribution; Fig 4b). Adapter dimers (~45 bp)
//   also generated and removed in the clean-up step below.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat tagmentationMix at 55c for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3a: Dispense SPRI magnetic bead droplet (4.5 uL) from
//   the clean-up module capillary onto the DMF hub. Beads
//   are Solid Phase Reversible Immobilisation (SPRI) beads
//   (Beckman Coulter) used to purify tagmented DNA and remove
//   excess enzyme, adapter dimers, and small fragments.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cleanupBeads    = dispense 1 units of MagneticBeads_SPRI

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3b: Merge tagmented product with SPRI beads on DMF
//   hub. The combined droplet is aspirated into the clean-up
//   module (capillary tubing, 160 um OD / 100 um ID,
//   inserted into the DMF air gap via side port).
//   External neodymium magnet (3 mm dia x 3 mm) positioned
//   below the module immobilises the bead pellet against the
//   inner tube wall. Positive pressure-driven syringe pump
//   flow (10 uL/min) achieves near-complete supernatant
//   removal from the pellet (Fig 3, frames 1-3).
//   Supernatant (excess enzyme + small DNA + adapter dimers)
//   is returned to DMF hub and actuated to waste capillary.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tagmentedBead   = mix tagmentationMix with cleanupBeads for 30s
dispose tagmentedBead

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Ethanol wash of bead pellet (x3).
//   Wash 1: 3 uL ethanol (100%) dispensed onto DMF hub,
//   aspirated into clean-up module, shuttled back-and-forth
//   for 30 s across the immobilised bead pellet (chaotic
//   mixing; removes trace contaminants / salts).
//   Ethanol is returned to DMF hub, actuated to waste module,
//   and aspirated off-chip. Procedure repeated twice more
//   (3 total washes) as per Nextera protocol.
//
//   NOTE: Each wash cycle uses a fresh 3 uL ethanol droplet.
//   Three separate wash droplets are modelled below to
//   reflect the sequential, independent wash boluses.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ethanolWash1    = dispense 1 units of EthanolWash
ethanolBolus1   = mix ethanolWash1 with ethanolWash1 for 30s
dispose ethanolBolus1

ethanolWash2    = dispense 1 units of EthanolWash
ethanolBolus2   = mix ethanolWash2 with ethanolWash2 for 30s
dispose ethanolBolus2

ethanolWash3    = dispense 1 units of EthanolWash
ethanolBolus3   = mix ethanolWash3 with ethanolWash3 for 30s
dispose ethanolBolus3

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Elution of clean tagmented DNA from bead pellet.
//   2.2 uL elution buffer (water + 0.1% Pluronic F127)
//   dispensed onto DMF hub and aspirated into clean-up module.
//   External magnet removed; beads resuspended in buffer by
//   back-and-forth bolus shuttling for 30 s at room temperature.
//   Magnet re-applied to immobilise beads; the DNA-containing
//   eluate droplet returned to the DMF hub and actuated to
//   the PCR inlet electrode.
//   Product: 2.2 uL purified, adapter-tagged DNA fragments.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

elutionBuf1     = dispense 1 units of ElutionBuffer
cleanedDNA      = mix elutionBuf1 with elutionBuf1 for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6a: Dispense PCR Mixture (2.8 uL) from its capillary.
//   Contents: 12.5 uL 2X PCR buffer + 0.5 uL primer cocktail
//   + 0.5 uL PCR enzyme + 0.5 uL 50X Adapter 2 (per well
//   per manufacturer; scaled to 2.8 uL on-chip volume).
//   This mixture adds Illumina-specific dual-indexed adapters
//   to the fragment ends via limited-cycle PCR amplification.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pcrMix          = dispense 1 units of PCRMixture

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6b: Merge eluate with PCR mixture on DMF hub (30 s).
//   The combined ~5 uL droplet is then aspirated into the
//   PCR thermal module: 2.8 uL enters the module inlet;
//   remaining 2.2 uL actuated to waste on DMF hub.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

prePCRDroplet   = mix cleanedDNA with pcrMix for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6c: Limited-cycle PCR - adapter addition and enrichment.
//   Thermocycling conditions (OpenPCR benchtop cycler via
//   Al block; closed-loop PID temperature control):
//     Initial extension:  72 C for 3 min
//     Denaturation:       95 C for 30 s
//     10 cycles:
//       Denaturation:     95 C for 10 s
//       Annealing:        62 C for 30 s
//       Extension:        72 C for 3 min
//   After PCR the product is dispensed back onto DMF hub
//   for size selection.
//   Product (Fig 4c): broad ~200-10000 bp enriched library
//   with primer dimers (~55 bp) to be removed by size selection.
//
//   NOTE: BioScript `heat` models one temperature phase per
//   call. The full thermocycling program is abstracted as
//   sequential heat steps (init extension, denaturation,
//   and the rate-limiting 10-cycle block at the annealing
//   temperature as the combined incubation).
//   10 cycles x (10s + 30s + 180s) = 10 cycles x 220s = 2200s.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat prePCRDroplet at 72c for 3m
heat prePCRDroplet at 95c for 30s
heat prePCRDroplet at 62c for 2200s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7a: Size Selection - Stage 1 (remove fragments <200 bp).
//   PCR product dispensed back to DMF hub from PCR module.
//   Merge with 2.2 uL SPRI beads (high bead:DNA ratio to
//   bind all DNA including primer dimers and small fragments).
//   Aspirate into size-selection module. Immobilise beads
//   with external magnet; supernatant (contains desired
//   200-400 bp fragments) returned to DMF hub.
//
//   NOTE: The supernatant -- not the bead-bound fraction --
//   carries the size-selected library at this stage (binding
//   conditions set to leave 200-400 bp fragments in solution).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sizeSelBeads1   = dispense 1 units of MagneticBeads_SPRI
sizeSelMix1     = mix prePCRDroplet with sizeSelBeads1 for 30s

// Supernatant (200-400 bp library) recovered from Stage 1.
// Bead pellet (small DNA + primer dimers) disposed.
librarySuper    = mix sizeSelMix1 with sizeSelMix1 for 10s
dispose sizeSelMix1

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7b: Size Selection - Stage 2 (remove fragments >400 bp).
//   The supernatant from Stage 1 is merged with 0.45 uL SPRI
//   beads (low bead:DNA ratio to bind only large fragments
//   >400 bp). Beads immobilised; ethanol wash performed on
//   bead pellet (large DNA + residual contaminants disposed).
//   Final elution: 3 uL elution buffer resuspends the desired
//   200-400 bp library from the Stage-2 bead pellet; eluate
//   returned to DMF hub as the final sequencer-ready library.
//
//   NOTE: At Stage 2 the DESIRED library is bead-bound (large
//   fragments captured; smaller fragments remain in solution
//   and are disposed). Elution releases the 200-400 bp library.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sizeSelBeads2   = dispense 1 units of MagneticBeads_SPRI
sizeSelMix2     = mix librarySuper with sizeSelBeads2 for 30s

// Ethanol wash of Stage-2 bead pellet (200-400 bp library bound).
ethanolSS       = dispense 1 units of EthanolWash
sizeSelWash     = mix sizeSelMix2 with ethanolSS for 30s
dispose sizeSelWash

// Elute final library (3 uL elution buffer) from Stage-2 beads.
elutionBuf2     = dispense 1 units of ElutionBuffer
dnaLibrary      = mix elutionBuf2 with elutionBuf2 for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Library QC detection.
//   Final library droplet (3 uL, target 200-400 bp) dispensed
//   back to DMF hub for analysis.
//   On-chip QC abstracts the Bioanalyzer (Agilent) size
//   distribution check (Fig 4d) and Kapa library quantification
//   kit fluorescence-based quantitation step (off-chip).
//   Passing criterion: library peak in 200-400 bp window
//   at sufficient concentration for MiSeq loading (8 pM).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

librarySignal   = detect libraryQC on dnaLibrary for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Library QC gate
// Pass (BB2): librarySignal > 0 -> valid 200-400 bp library
//             at sequencer-compatible concentration; dispose
//             for off-chip MiSeq loading (300-cycle paired-end
//             150 bp kit, loading concentration 8 pM).
// Fail (BB3): librarySignal <= 0 -> library preparation
//             failed (insufficient size selection, low yield,
//             or under/over-clustering risk); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (librarySignal > 0) {
    dispose dnaLibrary
} else {
    drain dnaLibrary
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose library QC signal droplet.
// Sequencer-ready library available off-chip for MiSeq run.
// Total on-chip time: ~1 h (5 min hands-on).
// ============================================================

dispose librarySignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
